# The pinned BLIS stack: the ONE source of truth for "which simulator priced these reports".
#
# Read by scripts/build_catalog.py and every workflow in .github/workflows/; SETUP.md documents
# the same pins for a human cloning by hand.
#
# Shell-sourceable (`set -a; . pins.env; set +a`) and parsed as plain KEY=VALUE by Python, so
# keep to unquoted, comment-or-assignment lines.
#
# Bumping a pin is automated: bump-blis-pin.yml opens a DRAFT PR (`scripts/blis_pin.py bump`),
# pin-compat.yml gates it, and merging runs regen-reports.yml. By hand: change BLIS_REF/BLIS_SHA,
# run `python3 -I scripts/sync_pins.py` for the derived block, then `scripts/test_build.py`.

# The release whose binary prices every run. BLIS_SHA is a COMMIT, and deliberately not a binary
# digest: the same tag builds to different bytes per toolchain, so a pinned digest would be wrong
# for every contributor but its author. The runners resolve the binary's SOURCE commit and compare
# that. Upstream tags are mutable, so CI refuses a moved tag outright while a local sweep only
# warns -- testing against an unreleased simulator is how a pin bump gets evaluated.
# Release v0.17.0: the squash merge of inference-sim's combined M2 pull request (#2118). It has
# `blis router-configs --json` and the per-GPU throughput figures in the Result.
# BLIS_REF names the tag the runners clone and BLIS_SHA the commit they require; a moved tag is refused.
BLIS_REF=v0.17.0
BLIS_SHA=c79c745619b16a8019339e3bbc79ee5e2923b258

# The router's reference EndpointPicker configs and their index are embedded in the pinned simulator and
# read with `blis router-configs --json`; they have no pin of their own (BLIS_SHA determines them).

# The catalog and registry a committed report is priced with are the ones EMBEDDED in the pinned
# simulator release (CFG-1): the binary is run with no --catalog or --registry, and every Result
# records data source "embedded". They have no pin of their own. The scripts that read catalog and
# registry FILES (workload descriptors, model graphs) read them from a blis-substrate checkout at
# SUBSTRATE_REF below, which is the same data.

# blis-substrate / blis-vllm / llm-d-router are NOT pinned by hand: they are Go dependencies
# compiled into the simulator, so BLIS_SHA already determines them. sync_pins.py derives them from
# inference-sim's go.mod at BLIS_SHA into the block below.

# >>> derived from inference-sim's go.mod at BLIS_REF -- DO NOT EDIT BY HAND >>>
# Regenerate with: python3 -I scripts/sync_pins.py  (after changing BLIS_REF above)
# Guarded by test_build.py::test_derived_pins_match_gomod.
SUBSTRATE_REF=v0.14.0
VLLM_REF=v0.32.0-blis.3
ROUTER_REF=v1.0.0-blis.4
# <<< end derived block <<<
